IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc24-appeal-scc`

-- ccc24-tests-appeal-scc.l4 -- tests for ccc24-appeal-scc.l4 (Criminal Code ss 691 to 696).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section, row by row, before the run.  T = JUST TRUE, F = JUST FALSE, N = NOTHING.

§ `Sections 691 and 692`

-- 691(1): convicted of an indictable offence, conviction affirmed; ground (a) dissent on a question of law, or (b) leave on a question of law.
#ASSERT `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) dissent
#ASSERT `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) leave
#ASSERT `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- neither ground
#ASSERT `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not convicted of an indictable offence
#ASSERT `s 691(1) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the conviction was not affirmed
-- 691(2): arguments are (acquitted of an indictable offence, acquitted by NCR verdict, acquittal set aside, question of law, dissent, guilty verdict entered, leave).
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) the Court of Appeal enters a verdict of guilty
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- acquitted by reason of a verdict of not criminally responsible: excluded
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the acquittal was not set aside
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 691(2) the person may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada against the setting aside of the acquittal` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not on a question of law
#ASSERT `s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a) the verdict is affirmed
#ASSERT `s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b) a guilty verdict is entered under 686(4)(b)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 692(1) the person found not criminally responsible may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 692(2) the person found unfit to stand trial may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 692(2) the person found unfit to stand trial may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 692(2) the person found unfit to stand trial may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 692(3) an appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be on the ground` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 692(3) an appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be on the ground` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 692(3) an appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be on the ground` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 692(3) an appeal under subsection (1) or (2) may be on the ground` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an appeal under (1) or (2)

§ `Sections 693 to 696`

#ASSERT `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no ground
#ASSERT `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 693(1) the Attorney General may appeal to the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the judgment is not one the subsection names: "Where a judgment of a court of appeal sets aside a conviction"
#ASSERT `s 693(2) the Supreme Court of Canada may impose such terms as it sees fit on the grant of leave to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 693(2) the Supreme Court of Canada may impose such terms as it sees fit on the grant of leave to appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694 notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694 notice of appeal in writing has been served by the appellant on the respondent in accordance with the Supreme Court Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "No appeal lies ... unless notice of appeal in writing is served"
#ASSERT `s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(1) the Supreme Court of Canada or a judge may assign counsel to act on behalf of an accused who is a party to an appeal to the Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(2) the fees and disbursements of the assigned counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General who is the appellant or respondent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(2) the fees and disbursements of the assigned counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General who is the appellant or respondent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(2) the fees and disbursements of the assigned counsel shall be paid by the Attorney General who is the appellant or respondent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(3) the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the Registrar of the Supreme Court of Canada to tax the disputed fees and disbursements` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(3) the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the Registrar of the Supreme Court of Canada to tax the disputed fees and disbursements` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 694.1(3) the Attorney General or the counsel may apply to the Registrar of the Supreme Court of Canada to tax the disputed fees and disbursements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

`ccc24 fixture 694a` MEANS `s 694.2(2)(a) an application for leave to appeal`
`ccc24 fixture 694b` MEANS `s 694.2(2)(b) a proceeding that is preliminary or incidental to an appeal`
`ccc24 fixture 694c` MEANS `s 694.2(2)(c) the hearing of the appeal`
`ccc24 fixture 694x` MEANS `s 694.2(2) another proceeding`

#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694a` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694b` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694c` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- unlike section 688, the hearing itself is in the list
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694c` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- rules of court provide that entitlement
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694c` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the Court or a judge gives leave
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` TRUE `ccc24 fixture 694x` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 694.2(2) the bar on a represented appellant in custody being present before the Supreme Court of Canada applies` FALSE `ccc24 fixture 694c` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "Subject to subsection (2)"
#ASSERT `s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the bar is not engaged: the entitlement stands
#ASSERT `s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- does not desire to be present: outside the relative clause
#ASSERT `s 694.2(1) an appellant who is in custody is entitled to be present at the hearing of the appeal before the Supreme Court of Canada` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 695(1) the Supreme Court of Canada may make any order that the court of appeal might have made and any rule or order that is necessary to give effect to its judgment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 695(1) the Supreme Court of Canada may make any order that the court of appeal might have made and any rule or order that is necessary to give effect to its judgment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the accused may elect to have the new trial ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the accused may elect to have the new trial ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no consent of the prosecutor
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the accused may elect to have the new trial ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- in Nunavut: (3) governs
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the accused may elect to have the new trial ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury or a provincial court judge` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a judge-and-jury new trial
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the election is deemed to be a re-election within the meaning of subsection 561(5) and subsections 561(5) to (7) apply to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 695(2) the election is deemed to be a re-election within the meaning of subsection 561(5) and subsections 561(5) to (7) apply to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 695(3) the accused may elect to have the new trial in Nunavut ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 695(3) the accused may elect to have the new trial in Nunavut ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 695(3) the accused may elect to have the new trial in Nunavut ordered by the Supreme Court of Canada heard before a judge without a jury` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 695(3) the election is deemed to be a re-election within the meaning of subsection 561.1(6) and subsections 561.1(6) to (9) apply to it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 695(3) the election is deemed to be a re-election within the meaning of subsection 561.1(6) and subsections 561.1(6) to (9) apply to it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696 the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province has under Part XXI` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 696 the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province has under Part XXI` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 696 the Attorney General of Canada has the same rights of appeal as the Attorney General of a province has under Part XXI` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
